faqs:
  - q: How does online booking help reduce no-shows?
    a: Our booking system sends automated text and email reminders before each appointment. Clients can confirm, reschedule, or cancel with a single tap. You can also require credit card holds or deposits for high-value services. Combined, these features reduce no-shows by up to 90 percent. That means fewer empty chairs and more predictable revenue every week.
  - q: Can I offer gift cards through my website?
    a: Yes. We build digital gift card systems directly into your website. Customers purchase gift cards online with instant email delivery to the recipient. Gift cards are tracked in your CRM so you always know balances and redemption history. Physical gift cards can also be integrated with the same system for in-salon purchases.
  - q: How does GullStack compare to Vagaro, GlossGenius, or Square for salons?
    a: Those platforms charge 2.5 to 3.5 percent on every transaction. On a $200 color service, that is $5 to $7 gone. Multiply that by hundreds of services per month and you are losing thousands per year. GullStack charges 1 percent for payment processing and includes booking, client management, and marketing automation. You get the same core features with dramatically lower fees.
  - q: Can stylists manage their own schedules?
    a: Yes. Each stylist or technician gets their own login to manage their availability, view upcoming appointments, and access client notes. They can block off personal time, set their own working hours, and see their daily schedule from their phone. The system handles multiple providers, different service durations, and varying availability without conflicts.
  - q: How do loyalty programs work with GullStack?
    a: We build custom loyalty programs tailored to your salon. Options include points-based systems where clients earn rewards for every visit, punch card style programs for specific services, referral bonuses for bringing in new clients, and birthday rewards. Everything is tracked automatically in your CRM so clients and staff never have to manage physical cards or remember point balances.
